      "id": 129412,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-26T14:26:34.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I feel like I'm missing something. I don't understand how providing more characters will make the draft/ban less useful or interesting.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>If someone takes Citizen Dawn right now, the most obvious counter is Omnitron because of its ability to move opponents, but that's not the only one. The Operative is pretty good at moving opponents, and I also played a match where we beat Dawn/Truth simply by being hard to incapacitate ourselves and having Baron Blade one shot Truth.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>But let's say that new characters really do make it so there are fewer situations in which there is an obvious counter to a character because there are many ways to counter the character. Isn't that even more interesting? Isn't that more interesting than the choice for how to counter a character being so obvious that we end up with a lot of the same characters over and over again?</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:04:20.938Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
